{
  "id": "MECH-QUERIES-B",
  "board_entry": "B-CASCADE",
  "variable_under_test": "MAX_QUERIES_PER_HEAD n jointly with DELTA_WEIGHT w(n)=1e-2*n/64, i.e. the trust region's RELATIVE pull is held constant instead of decaying like 1/n. All else canonical EXP-007-top32 at TOP_T=32.",
  "why": "MECH-QUERIES swept n at FIXED w=1e-2. The guarded solve stacks [X_new (n x t); sqrt(w) I (t x t)], so the data Gram grows with n while the trust region contributes a fixed t rows and its relative pull decays like 1/n. That confounds 'more queries do not help' with 'more queries help but the vanishing trust region cancels it'. Scaling w with n removes the confound, env-only.",
  "import_pin": {
    "snapshot_dir": "/tmp/amsnap_mqb",
    "snapshot_commit": "58c30f3bac24f99416694711ac4aa38d3c6077e8",
